                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love the original Lucius, it's a janky. buggy mess that is just oh so compelling. Lucius II tried something else, but ended up quite boring. At least there was an attempt at something there. The demake is maybe the best example of a faithful adaptation you'll ever see.\n\nAnd with that I say do not play Lucius III.  It seems like a return to normalcy, it seems like we're going back to the old formula. Figuring out the steps to get to a cinematic death scene. And it'll be fine for a while. You start to worry about the devs outlooks on life, but not more than you did when you were playing the second one. It'll be buggy here and there, but nothing worse than you're used of from the original Lucius.\n\nThe worst part is that you might enjoy playing Lucius III for a bit. And when you think to yourself \"Oh, we seem to be about halfway, I can't wait for the rest.\" the game ends. THIS GAME IS UNFINISHED. Effectively three whole chapters were lost. There's some optional murders that are easily missed that would've probably been part of the main story. They should have been. Even the writing alludes to the fact that we skipped three chapters. It's JARRING. And wherever you though the pitch of \"evil devil child murders his whole family and later an entire town\" would go to, you will be left disappointed with the direction this game takes by the end. \n\nI like pretending the sequels don't exist. The original Lucius is great. I'm glad I discovered what the sequels were all about. I see why this dev team seems to have disbanded. Let the franchise fizzle out. Lucius will not be back and I am fine with this.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1788550621,
